"""Orville Swanson, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 1 to 6, epilogue 1907).

Sources (Red Dead Wiki EN, Oct 2026, saved in scratchpad cov/orville/, cov/orville/m/ and cov/orville/w/): character
page "Orville Swanson" (Background, Events of Red Dead Redemption 2, Mission Appearances, Trivia); FR page "Orville
Swanson" (fr.txt: confirms San Francisco and the ship to Shanghai, the move to New York, the Ledger article);
transcripts "Outlaws from the West/dialogues" (Davey lines), "Who the Hell is Leviticus Cornwall?/dialogues" (John's
bedside), "Eastward Bound/dialogues" (loading the wagon, "no more passengers", Hosea's "Swanson found something... down
at the train station by the lake", "A couple of weeks later"), "Who is Not Without Sin/dialogues" (whole mission, camp
comments), "Blessed are the Peacemakers/dialogues" (Arthur's return and the later exchange); mission pages "Who is
Not Without Sin" (Luther and Marvin, five hands, the shepherd witness, Bard's Crossing), "Blessed are the
Peacemakers" (several weeks before Swanson speaks to Arthur), "A Strange Kindness", "Blood Feuds, Ancient and
Modern", "The Battle of Shady Belle", "Horsemen, Apocalypses" (story: Charles, Swanson and Pearson bury Kieran;
trivia: Swanson hides in Hosea's room), "Fleeting Joy", "That's Murfree Country", "A Rage Unleashed" (story: brief
talk with Swanson, Dutch interrupts), "The Fine Art of Conversation" (story and trivia: the Swanson or Calderón
condition, Swanson and Trelawny gone from camp afterwards), "Red Dead Redemption (mission)" (recalled line);
"Camp Events" (Hosea campfire: bigamy; Shady Belle: the monk and the college days); "Brother Dorkins" (Arthur first
hears of him from Swanson); newspaper article "Reverend Swanson Leads NY Church" (full text) and "Blackwater Ledger
No. 74"; "Lakay". Second source for the Emerald Station scene, which has no transcript on the wiki (checked Oct 2026,
"The Fine Art of Conversation/dialogues" and "A Rage Unleashed/dialogues" do not exist): ireddead.com guide "The Fine
Art of Conversation" (bench, women and Jack refuse to come, honor variants, handshake on low honor) and ireddead.com
"A Rage Unleashed" (a cleaned-up Swanson at the start of the mission).
Cross-checked against the fact-checked parts: arthur_A (Who is Not Without Sin), arthur_C (A Rage Unleashed, Emerald
Station), john_A (bedside), dutch_A/dutch_C (saved Dutch's life, never explained; "no more passengers"; Blessed),
charles_A/charles_B (Bare Knuckle Friendships; Charles's news of Swanson attributed to the Red Dead Wiki), kieran_A
(burial by Charles, Swanson and Pearson), uncle rules (Milton's three days conditional on Dutch's surrender; Shady Belle
cleared of Lemoyne Raiders), susan/karen/tilly fc reports (camp comments in "Who is Not Without Sin" are optional,
only if Arthur greets people).

Ownership: Rockstar's description and the official guide text (B, Personality), names and nicknames (B), appearance and
the fake bible (B), camp scenes (Isaiah reading, Micah's bullying and Susan, Strauss and the loan, Javier's prayer,
Bill, Uncle's mooning, the fire speech, the party, the ghost in the swamp, the Beaver Hollow talks with Arthur and
Strauss, his approval of Strauss's exile) go to part B; this part refers to them in one clause at most. Part A OWNS
the backstory he tells himself (marriage, bigamy, San Francisco, Shanghai) and the newspaper article. Lines quoted in part C are paraphrased here without quotation marks.

Excluded: "Just another of sins to add to the list" (no transcript); the wiki claim that he "eventually chooses to
leave the gang due to its inevitable collapse" as a motive in our voice (his reasons are given as he states them at
Emerald Station, from two sources); what he did during the Saint Denis bank robbery and the weeks at Lakay (not shown);
who Margaret is (never said); the official guide's account of how his morphine use began (guide text, part B); "Of Men and Angels" versus ireddead's "Brothers and Sisters, One and All" as the condition (the
wiki's mission page and character page both say "Of Men and Angels": kept); Charles's news of Swanson stated as fact
(no transcript for "Bare Knuckle Friendships": attributed to the Red Dead Wiki, as in charles_B); any date or place of
birth (none given).
Fact-check of 20 Oct 2026: at Emerald Station, everything from the single ireddead.com source is removed (bench,
"can no longer change Dutch's course", "trusts Arthur", "lived as a fighter", the handshake): only the leaving by
train, Dutch's behavior and "nonsense" (wiki, attributed), the refusal of the women and Jack (mission page and
character page), and the two attested lines are kept. The stranger at Bard's Crossing can be killed or knocked out
(mission page: "can be killed by Arthur to protect Swanson", no honor loss). The Brother Dorkins scene and the gang's
comments in "Who is Not Without Sin" (except Susan) are told in part B Relationships; this part points to them.
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The games give no date or place of birth for Orville Swanson. The Red Dead Wiki lists him as an American. Before he joined the Van der Linde gang he was a clergyman, a calling he lost along with his faith and his family. He once saved the life of [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] (see Personality).",
              "Les jeux ne donnent ni date ni lieu de naissance pour Orville Swanson. Le Red Dead Wiki le présente comme américain. Avant de rejoindre la bande Van der Linde, il était homme d'Église, une vocation qu'il a perdue en même temps que sa foi et sa famille. Il a un jour sauvé la vie de [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] (voir Personnalité).")},
    {"p": two("The rest of his past comes from his own account, given to [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] at the campfire at Horseshoe Overlook. Swanson married a woman who, as it turned out, already had a husband, which made him a bigamist without his knowing it. The police found the two of them in San Francisco. She sailed for Shanghai, and that was the last he saw of her. He tells Hosea that he supposes he is in some way still married.",
              "Le reste de son passé vient de son propre récit, fait à [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] autour du feu de camp de Horseshoe Overlook. Swanson a épousé une femme qui, il l'a appris ensuite, avait déjà un mari : il est donc devenu bigame sans le savoir. La police a retrouvé le couple à San Francisco. Elle a pris la mer pour Shanghai, et il ne l'a plus jamais revue. Il confie à Hosea qu'il se considère toujours plus ou moins marié.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 1: Colter", "Chapitre 1 : Colter"), "chapter": 1},
    {"p": two("The game opens in \"Outlaws from the West\", with the gang's wagons crossing the Grizzlies in a snowstorm after the failed ferry robbery in Blackwater. Swanson climbs down from a wagon and walks up to Dutch. He tells him that [[abigail-marston|Abigail]] thinks Davey Callander, wounded in Blackwater, is dying, and that they will have to stop somewhere. Dutch answers that he has sent [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] ahead to look for shelter. The gang takes refuge in the abandoned mining town of Colter. There, Abigail announces that Davey is dead, and Swanson tells her she could not have done anything more for him.",
              "Le jeu s'ouvre sur \"Outlaws from the West\" : les chariots de la bande traversent les Grizzlies en pleine tempête de neige, après l'échec du braquage du ferry à Blackwater. Swanson descend d'un chariot et rejoint Dutch. Il lui rapporte qu'[[abigail-marston|Abigail]] juge Davey Callander, blessé à Blackwater, mourant, et qu'il va falloir s'arrêter quelque part. Dutch répond qu'il a envoyé [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] en éclaireur chercher un abri. La bande se réfugie dans Colter, une ville minière abandonnée. Là, Abigail annonce la mort de Davey, et Swanson lui assure qu'elle n'aurait rien pu faire de plus.")},
    {"p": two("While the armed men go out on jobs, Swanson remains behind at Colter, along with [[uncle|Uncle]], [[simon-pearson|Pearson]], [[leopold-strauss|Strauss]], [[jack-marston|Jack]] and the women (his camp scenes there are in Relationships). At the start of \"Who the Hell is Leviticus Cornwall?\", he is sitting at the bedside of [[john-marston|John Marston]], who was mauled by wolves in the mountains. Arthur, already in the cabin, jokes that he had expected Swanson to be reading John his last rites, but sees him sharing his \"other passion\" instead. Swanson stands, demands a little respect and leaves the cabin.",
              "Quand les hommes armés partent en expédition, Swanson reste à Colter avec [[uncle|Uncle]], [[simon-pearson|Pearson]], [[leopold-strauss|Strauss]], [[jack-marston|Jack]] et les femmes (ses scènes de camp figurent dans Relations). Au début de \"Who the Hell is Leviticus Cornwall?\", il est assis au chevet de [[john-marston|John Marston]], blessé par des loups dans la montagne. Arthur, déjà dans la cabane, lance qu'il croyait le trouver en train d'administrer les derniers sacrements à John, mais qu'il le voit plutôt lui faire découvrir son \"autre passion\". Swanson se lève, exige un peu de respect et quitte la cabane.")},
    {"p": two("When the snow melts, the gang leaves the mountains in \"Eastward Bound\". As Hosea proposes Horseshoe Overlook, near Valentine, as the next camp, Swanson is loading supplies into a wagon with [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]]. At the new camp, Dutch gathers everyone, tells them it is time to earn money and singles out Uncle and Swanson: the gang will carry no more passengers. Some of the others laugh.",
              "Quand la neige fond, la bande quitte les montagnes dans \"Eastward Bound\". Pendant qu'Hosea propose Horseshoe Overlook, près de Valentine, pour le prochain camp, Swanson charge des provisions dans un chariot avec [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]]. Au nouveau camp, Dutch rassemble tout le monde, annonce qu'il est temps de gagner de l'argent et vise nommément Uncle et Swanson : la bande ne transportera plus de passagers. Quelques membres éclatent de rire.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 2: Horseshoe Overlook", "Chapitre 2 : Horseshoe Overlook"), "chapter": 2},
    {"p": two("A couple of weeks later, Hosea tells Arthur that Swanson has found something at the train station by the lake. In \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur rides to Flatneck Station, in the Heartlands, and finds Swanson very drunk at a poker table with two men, Luther and Marvin. Swanson greets him by announcing that he has followed Arthur's advice and broken free of morphine. Arthur answers that he looks drunk rather than free. Luther insists that the reverend finish the game. Swanson calls the two players good men and children of God, then collapses on the floor.",
              "Une quinzaine de jours plus tard, Hosea apprend à Arthur que Swanson a trouvé quelque chose à la gare, au bord du lac. Dans \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur se rend à Flatneck Station, dans les Heartlands, et y trouve Swanson ivre mort à une table de poker, avec deux hommes, Luther et Marvin. Swanson l'accueille en annonçant qu'il a suivi son conseil et s'est libéré de la morphine. Arthur lui répond qu'il a l'air ivre plutôt que libre. Luther tient à ce que le révérend termine la partie. Swanson qualifie les deux joueurs de braves gens et d'enfants de Dieu, puis s'effondre par terre.")},
    {"p": two("Luther then suggests that Arthur play in Swanson's place. If he accepts, he plays up to five hands, and when Marvin mocks the reverend, Arthur tells him that Swanson is a decent man going through a bad time and warns him not to do it again. Whether he plays or not, Swanson crawls out of the building in the meantime. Arthur searches for him around the station and asks passers-by, who point him west. He finds Swanson in a fight with a stranger, who pushes the reverend away and turns on Arthur. Arthur can knock the man out or kill him; according to the mission page, killing him costs no honor. Arthur then runs down a shepherd who saw the fight and threatens him into keeping quiet.",
              "Luther propose alors à Arthur de jouer à la place de Swanson. S'il accepte, il dispute jusqu'à cinq mains, et quand Marvin se moque du révérend, Arthur lui répond que Swanson est un type bien qui traverse une mauvaise passe, et le prévient de ne pas recommencer. Qu'il joue ou non, Swanson en profite pour sortir à quatre pattes du bâtiment. Arthur le cherche autour de la gare et interroge des passants, qui lui indiquent l'ouest. Il trouve Swanson aux prises avec un inconnu, qui repousse le révérend et s'en prend à Arthur. Arthur peut l'assommer ou le tuer ; d'après la page de la mission, le tuer ne coûte aucun point d'honneur. Arthur rattrape ensuite un berger témoin de la bagarre et le menace pour qu'il se taise.")},
    {"p": two("Swanson has meanwhile wandered onto Bard's Crossing, the railway bridge over the Dakota River, and caught his foot in the track. Arthur climbs up to him, frees the foot as a train arrives, and the two get clear of the rails just in time. When Swanson thanks him, Arthur shoves him to the ground. Swanson protests at being thrown off a bridge, Arthur shouts that there was a train, and the reverend breaks down: he apologizes and says he wishes he were different. As Arthur offers to take him home, Swanson says he could have tea with Margaret, then passes out before he can say who she is.",
              "Pendant ce temps, Swanson s'est aventuré sur Bard's Crossing, le pont ferroviaire qui enjambe la Dakota, et s'est coincé le pied dans la voie. Arthur grimpe jusqu'à lui, dégage le pied au moment où un train arrive, et les deux hommes s'écartent des rails de justesse. Quand Swanson le remercie, Arthur le jette à terre. Swanson s'indigne qu'on l'ait poussé d'un pont, Arthur lui hurle qu'il y avait un train, et le révérend s'effondre : il s'excuse et dit qu'il aimerait être différent. Quand Arthur propose de le ramener chez lui, Swanson évoque un thé qu'il pourrait prendre avec Margaret, puis perd connaissance avant d'avoir dit qui elle est.")},
    {"p": two("Arthur carries him back to Horseshoe Overlook on his horse while Swanson mumbles about cards, kippers, tea and Margaret. If Arthur greets the others as he carries him through camp, most of them comment on the reverend's state (see Relationships). Arthur drops Swanson on his bed and leaves him in the care of [[susan-grimshaw|Susan Grimshaw]].",
              "Arthur le ramène à Horseshoe Overlook sur son cheval, pendant que Swanson marmonne des histoires de cartes, de harengs fumés, de thé et de Margaret. Si Arthur salue les autres en traversant le camp avec lui sur l'épaule, la plupart y vont de leur commentaire sur l'état du révérend (voir Relations). Arthur dépose Swanson sur son lit et le confie à [[susan-grimshaw|Susan Grimshaw]].")},
    {"p": two("At the end of the chapter, after \"A Strange Kindness\", the gang leaves Horseshoe Overlook for Clemens Point, on Flat Iron Lake in Lemoyne, and Swanson moves with it.",
              "À la fin du chapitre, après \"A Strange Kindness\", la bande quitte Horseshoe Overlook pour Clemens Point, au bord du lac Flat Iron, en Lemoyne, et Swanson la suit.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 3: Clemens Point", "Chapitre 3 : Clemens Point"), "chapter": 3},
    {"p": two("In \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", Arthur is captured and tortured by the O'Driscoll Boys during a parley between Dutch and [[colm-odriscoll|Colm O'Driscoll]]. He escapes and rides back to Clemens Point, where he collapses. Dutch calls for help from Miss Grimshaw, then for Swanson, who tells the wounded man that he is safe now. Arthur is put to bed, and Dutch asks Susan to sit with him. Several weeks pass before the closing scene, in which Swanson visits the recovering Arthur. He admits that he thought he would be burying him; Arthur replies that it is not time yet. The two wish each other well.",
              "Dans \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", Arthur est capturé et torturé par les O'Driscoll Boys pendant une rencontre entre Dutch et [[colm-odriscoll|Colm O'Driscoll]]. Il s'échappe et regagne Clemens Point, où il s'effondre. Dutch appelle Miss Grimshaw à l'aide, puis Swanson, qui rassure le blessé : il est en sécurité, maintenant. On met Arthur au lit, et Dutch demande à Susan de rester à son chevet. Plusieurs semaines s'écoulent avant la scène finale, où Swanson rend visite à Arthur, en convalescence. Il avoue qu'il pensait devoir l'enterrer ; Arthur répond que ce n'est pas encore pour cette fois. Les deux hommes se souhaitent bonne chance.")},
    {"p": two("The Red Dead Wiki also lists Swanson in the two missions that end the chapter, although their mission pages do not name him. In \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", Dutch and seven of his men ride to Braithwaite Manor in search of the kidnapped Jack, while the rest of the gang waits at Clemens Point. The next morning, in \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", the Pinkerton agents [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] and [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] walk into the camp. Milton offers the others three days to disappear, on condition that Dutch surrenders; the gang refuses. Arthur and John clear the abandoned Shady Belle plantation house of Lemoyne Raiders, and the gang moves into it.",
              "Le Red Dead Wiki cite aussi Swanson dans les deux missions qui closent le chapitre, même si leurs pages ne le nomment pas. Dans \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", Dutch et sept de ses hommes chevauchent jusqu'au manoir Braithwaite à la recherche de Jack, enlevé, pendant que le reste de la bande attend à Clemens Point. Le lendemain matin, dans \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", les agents de la Pinkerton [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] et [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] entrent dans le camp. Milton laisse trois jours aux autres pour disparaître, à condition que Dutch se rende ; la bande refuse. Arthur et John débarrassent la demeure abandonnée de Shady Belle des Lemoyne Raiders qui l'occupent, et la bande s'y installe.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("At Shady Belle, Swanson is the one who first tells Arthur about Brother Dorkins, a monk in Saint Denis who leads to the stranger mission \"Help a Brother Out\" (see Relationships).",
              "À Shady Belle, c'est Swanson qui, le premier, parle à Arthur de frère Dorkins, un moine de Saint-Denis par qui passe la mission d'étranger \"Help a Brother Out\" (voir Relations).")},
    {"p": two("In \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", the O'Driscolls send [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]] into the camp dead on a horse, beheaded and with his eyes gouged out, then attack Shady Belle. The members who do not fight take shelter inside the house; according to the mission page, Swanson hides in Hosea's room. Once the attackers are driven off, Dutch has [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]], Swanson and Pearson bury Kieran while Arthur and John clear away the bodies.",
              "Dans \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", les O'Driscoll renvoient au camp, sur un cheval, le cadavre de [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]], décapité et les yeux arrachés, puis attaquent Shady Belle. Les membres qui ne se battent pas s'abritent dans la maison ; selon la page de la mission, Swanson se cache dans la chambre d'Hosea. Une fois les assaillants repoussés, Dutch charge [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]], Swanson et Pearson d'enterrer Kieran pendant qu'Arthur et John évacuent les corps.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 5: Guarma", "Chapitre 5 : Guarma"), "chapter": 5},
    {"p": two("After the failed Saint Denis bank robbery at the end of chapter 4, in \"Banking, The Old American Art\", Dutch, Arthur, [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], Bill and [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] end up on the island of Guarma. The rest of the gang leaves Shady Belle for Lakay, an abandoned settlement in the bayou northwest of Saint Denis. In \"Fleeting Joy\", Arthur reaches Lakay and finds the others there. According to the Red Dead Wiki, Swanson has overcome his addictions by then. The reunion is cut short by a Pinkerton attack on the village. In \"That's Murfree Country\", Arthur and Charles find a new hideout at Beaver Hollow, in Roanoke Ridge, and the gang moves there, Swanson included.",
              "Après l'échec du braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis, à la fin du chapitre 4, dans \"Banking, The Old American Art\", Dutch, Arthur, [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], Bill et [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] échouent sur l'île de Guarma. Le reste de la bande quitte Shady Belle pour Lakay, un hameau abandonné du bayou, au nord-ouest de Saint-Denis. Dans \"Fleeting Joy\", Arthur rejoint Lakay et y retrouve les autres. Selon le Red Dead Wiki, Swanson est alors venu à bout de ses dépendances. Les retrouvailles tournent court : les Pinkerton attaquent le village. Dans \"That's Murfree Country\", Arthur et Charles dénichent une nouvelle planque à Beaver Hollow, dans le Roanoke Ridge, et la bande s'y installe, Swanson compris.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 6: Beaver Hollow", "Chapitre 6 : Beaver Hollow"), "chapter": 6},
    {"p": two("His talks with Arthur and Strauss at Beaver Hollow are told in Relationships. At the start of \"A Rage Unleashed\", Arthur is talking with him in camp when Dutch calls Arthur over and tells him that the gang will head north to New York before going to the tropics. The arrival of Eagle Flies, whose tribe's horses have been seized by the army, then sends Arthur, Dutch and Charles away from camp.",
              "Ses conversations avec Arthur et Strauss à Beaver Hollow figurent dans Relations. Au début de \"A Rage Unleashed\", Arthur discute avec lui au camp quand Dutch l'appelle pour lui annoncer que la bande va monter vers New York avant de partir pour les tropiques. L'arrivée d'Eagle Flies, dont l'armée a confisqué les chevaux de la tribu, éloigne ensuite Arthur, Dutch et Charles du camp.")},
    {"p": two("In \"The Fine Art of Conversation\", Arthur and Charles help Captain Lyndon Monroe escape the army to Emerald Station. After Monroe has left on a train, Arthur has a coughing fit on the platform. If he has completed the stranger mission \"Of Men and Angels\" and has high honor, he meets Sister Calderón there. Otherwise he meets Swanson, who is leaving the gang. According to the Red Dead Wiki, Swanson brings up Dutch's erratic behavior and says he will not die for his nonsense. He tried to persuade the women and Jack to leave with him, but they refused.",
              "Dans \"The Fine Art of Conversation\", Arthur et Charles aident le capitaine Lyndon Monroe à échapper à l'armée jusqu'à Emerald Station. Une fois Monroe parti en train, Arthur est pris d'une quinte de toux sur le quai. S'il a terminé la mission d'étranger \"Of Men and Angels\" et que son honneur est élevé, il y croise sœur Calderón. Sinon, il croise Swanson, qui quitte la bande. D'après le Red Dead Wiki, Swanson évoque le comportement erratique de Dutch et dit qu'il ne mourra pas pour ses absurdités. Il a essayé de convaincre les femmes et Jack de partir avec lui, mais ils ont refusé.")},
    {"p": two("What follows depends on Arthur's honor. With high honor, Swanson tells Arthur to save who he can, let the rest rot and look after himself. With low honor, he tells Arthur that he lived his way and will die his way. Swanson then boards the train. He does not appear again in 1899: after this mission, Swanson and [[josiah-trelawny|Josiah Trelawny]] are no longer in the Beaver Hollow camp, and if Arthur meets Sister Calderón instead, Swanson's departure is not shown. With high honor, Arthur recalls Swanson's advice during his last ride in \"Red Dead Redemption\", at the end of the chapter.",
              "La suite dépend de l'honneur d'Arthur. Avec un honneur élevé, Swanson lui conseille de sauver ceux qu'il peut, de laisser les autres à leur sort et de prendre soin de lui. Avec un honneur bas, il lui dit qu'il a vécu à sa manière et qu'il mourra de même. Swanson monte ensuite dans le train. On ne le revoit plus en 1899 : après cette mission, Swanson et [[josiah-trelawny|Josiah Trelawny]] ont quitté le camp de Beaver Hollow, et si Arthur rencontre sœur Calderón à sa place, le départ de Swanson n'est pas montré. Avec un honneur élevé, Arthur se remémore le conseil de Swanson pendant sa dernière chevauchée, dans \"Red Dead Redemption\", à la fin du chapitre.")},

    # ================================================================ Epilogue 1907
    {"h3": two("Epilogue (1907)", "Épilogue (1907)"), "year": "1907"},
    {"h4": two("Epilogue 2: Beecher's Hope", "Épilogue 2 : Beecher's Hope"), "chapter": "E2"},
    {"p": two("Swanson does not appear in the epilogue. What became of him is told by others. According to the Red Dead Wiki, after John and Uncle find Charles in Saint Denis in \"Bare Knuckle Friendships\", Charles tells John that Swanson has moved to New York to become a preacher. An in-game newspaper article titled \"Reverend Swanson Leads NY Church\", printed in the Blackwater Ledger (No. 74), the New Hanover Gazette (No. 39) and the Saint Denis Times (No. 55), reports that he has been installed as minister of the First Congregational Church of New York, having moved to the city to take the post.",
              "Swanson n'apparaît pas dans l'épilogue. Ce qu'il est devenu, ce sont d'autres qui le racontent. Selon le Red Dead Wiki, après que John et Uncle ont retrouvé Charles à Saint-Denis dans \"Bare Knuckle Friendships\", Charles apprend à John que Swanson est parti à New York pour devenir prédicateur. Un article de presse du jeu, intitulé \"Reverend Swanson Leads NY Church\", publié dans le Blackwater Ledger (n° 74), la New Hanover Gazette (n° 39) et le Saint Denis Times (n° 55), annonce qu'il a été officiellement installé comme pasteur de la First Congregational Church de New York, ville où il s'est établi pour prendre ce poste.")},
    {"p": two("According to the article, a service and then a reception were held for his appointment. People who attended described his sermon, on acknowledging sin and seeking redemption, as \"impassioned and heartfelt\". In it he spoke of the period when he broke with his faith, could not attend church and fell into depravity. He then described how he found his faith again and began preaching on street corners, before becoming assistant pastor of a church in Ohio. At a recent convention of First Congregational Churches, his speech impressed those present, and he was offered the New York post almost at once.",
              "D'après l'article, un office puis une réception ont marqué sa nomination. Les fidèles présents ont trouvé son sermon, consacré à la reconnaissance du péché et à la quête de la rédemption, \"impassioned and heartfelt\" (passionné et sincère). Il y a évoqué la période où il avait rompu avec sa foi, ne pouvait plus mettre les pieds à l'église et avait sombré dans la débauche. Il a ensuite raconté comment il avait retrouvé la foi et s'était mis à prêcher au coin des rues, avant de devenir pasteur adjoint d'une église de l'Ohio. Lors d'un récent congrès des First Congregational Churches, son discours a frappé l'assistance, et le poste new-yorkais lui a été proposé presque aussitôt.")},
]
